{
  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "Microsoft Sentinel incident → AKSI control ID mapping. Microsoft Sentinel is Azure's cloud-native SIEM (parallel to Splunk on the Microsoft side of the SOC). Each incident's severity, status, classification, MITRE ATT&CK tactics/techniques, alert categories, automated-response (Sentinel playbook) governance fields, and AI-incident labels select a control. High-severity open incidents (status New/Active) become DE-01 FAIL (open high incident); High resolved+TruePositive becomes PR-05 FAIL (confirmed real incident requiring audit-trail closure evidence); High closed+FalsePositive becomes PR-05 PASS. Alerts categorised as Exfiltration become PR-04 FAIL; CredentialAccess becomes PR-01 FAIL; PrivilegeEscalation becomes PR-02 FAIL; Impact becomes DE-01 FAIL. MITRE techniques drive control selection via mitre_technique_to_control. Sentinel playbook autonomy fields (automatedResponse.playbook_executed, approval_required, approved_by, actions_taken) drive PR-02/PR-05 governance: high-impact actions executed without required approval become PR-02 FAIL; properly approved playbook executions become PR-05 PASS. AI-related labels (ai-related, prompt-injection, ai-incident, ml-attack) are captured for AI-agent-specific incident tracking, parallel to Splunk's category=AI/ML.",
  "_metadata": {
    "source_format": "microsoft_sentinel",
    "schema": "microsoft-graph-security-incidents-v0",
    "owner": "ancilis-importers",
    "spec_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/security-incident",
